# Coding & documentation — fieldops-app

Architecture and import boundaries live in `000-architecture.mdc`. This file covers how code is written and documented inside those layers.

## TypeScript

- `strict: true` in tsconfig. No `any` — use `unknown` and narrow, or generics.
- No non-null assertions (`!`) outside test files.
- Prefer discriminated unions for UI state machines:
  `{ status: 'idle' } | { status: 'loading' } | { status: 'empty' } | { status: 'error'; error: Error } | { status: 'success'; data: T }`
  Empty and error must remain distinguishable.

## React / React Native

- Function components only.
- Screens are presentational: call one ViewModel hook; render from its return value.
- No side effects in render. `useEffect` synchronizes with external systems; derived values are computed inline or with `useMemo` when justified.
- Accessibility props on interactive UI (`accessibilityRole`, `accessibilityLabel`, `accessibilityState`).
- Boolean props are predicates: `isDisabled`, `isLoading`.
- Prefer named exports. File name matches the primary export.

## Performance (guardrails — decide concrete approach at feature time)

- Keep scroll and typing jank-free; avoid heavy work on the JS thread during list interaction.
- Virtualize long lists (`FlatList` / FlashList when chosen). Append cursor pages; do not rebuild the whole list from scratch on every keystroke if avoidable.
- Prefer **server query params** (`q`, `status`) for filter/search over filtering a huge in-memory copy as the primary model.
- Stable `keyExtractor` ids — avoid index keys for paginated data.
- `React.memo` on row/item components when props are stable; `useCallback` for `renderItem` / handlers passed to memo children; `useMemo` for expensive or referential derived data. **Do not** blanket-memo everything — use when list or profiler shows churn.
- Keep filter/search state in the ViewModel; list data from Query cache. Do not duplicate the server list into parallel `useState` arrays just to filter unless deliberate and logged in `DECISIONS.md`.
- Debounce search input before changing query keys; guard infinite `fetchNextPage` against double fetch.
- Isolate form fields so typing one field does not re-render the entire screen tree when avoidable.
- When animation is added: prefer `useNativeDriver: true` where supported; Reanimated worklets for continuous/gesture animation. Do not animate by remounting large lists on the JS thread.

## DRY without speculative abstraction

- Duplication across two call sites is acceptable. On the third, extract into `core/utils`, `core/types`, or an integration port.
- Do not invent a generic abstraction for a single use site.
- Types placement law: see `000-architecture.mdc` (`core/types` vs feature `types/`).

## Lint & format

- ESLint with type-aware TypeScript rules and `eslint-plugin-react-hooks` when configured.
- Do not silence lint with `eslint-disable` as a first resort.

## Documentation — exports

Use full TSDoc on every exported hook, port, type helper in `core/types` or feature `types/`, and public utility: purpose, params, returns, `@remarks` for non-obvious behaviour.

## Documentation — internal logic (required)

Document non-trivial internal functions in **both** places:

1. **Above the function** — short block stating purpose and why this approach.
2. **Inside the function** — inline `//` on non-obvious branches (optimistic rollback, 409 handling, cursor page merge, 422 map). Explain reasoning, not narration of obvious code.

Same standard applies to **test files** that encode non-obvious setup or assert intent. Placement of tests: see `020-testing.mdc` (`tests/` mirror, not under `src/features`).

Skip noise on one-line obvious helpers.

## Decisions

When choosing list virtualization, debounce strategy, 409 UX, or integration shapes, update `DECISIONS.md` in the same turn per `030-decisions.mdc`.
